# This is the build context Docker actually uses for this service
# (docker-compose.yaml: factory-twin-3d.build.context: ./services/
# factory-twin-3d) -- a .dockerignore at the repo root does NOT apply
# here, since Docker only honors one in the context root itself. This
# file is the one that actually matters for this service's isolation.
#
# Defense-in-depth, not a replacement for the Dockerfile's existing
# explicit allowlist COPY (COPY server.js / COPY lib / COPY public --
# never COPY . .). If that ever changes to a wildcard COPY, this file is
# what stops private/ from being sent to the Docker daemon at all, before
# any COPY instruction could act on it.
private/
node_modules/
